From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:34:03 +0200
Subject: settings: viewing range 120 by default on the PS3, not 190

Luanti's default viewing range of 190 nodes is more than 217 MB of RAM
and the PPE can generate, mesh and draw: the benchmark flight over a
fresh world (gamedb:luanti's recipe, variant view190) ran at 15 fps
steady with 56 s of frames over 100 ms in its 135 s window and a 1% low
of 3 fps. 120 keeps most of the distance: 20 fps, 36 s of stalls and a 1%
low of 4 fps (3 runs, same boot, 2026-10-29), against 46 fps, 4.5 s and
17 fps at 60. 120 is a floor the user set (no lower graphics quality; the
stalls are to be fixed in the engine, gamedb:luanti todo.toml), not the
smoothest value. The Settings menu and a minetest.conf that names
viewing_range still change it.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/defaultsettings.cpp b/src/defaultsettings.cpp
--- a/src/defaultsettings.cpp
+++ b/src/defaultsettings.cpp
@@ -245,7 +245,10 @@ void set_default_settings()
 	settings->setDefault("tooltip_append_itemname", "false");
 	settings->setDefault("fps_max", "60");
 	settings->setDefault("fps_max_unfocused", "10");
-	settings->setDefault("viewing_range", "190");
+	// Walnut (PS3): 120, not 190: at 190 the fresh world flight ran at 15 fps with 56 s of stalls in
+	// 135 s, at 120 at 20 fps with 36 s, at 60 at 46 fps with 4.5 s (2026-10-28/29); 217 MB of RAM
+	// and the PPE set it, 120 is the lowest we accept (no lower graphics quality)
+	settings->setDefault("viewing_range", "120");
 	settings->setDefault("client_mesh_chunk", "1");
 	settings->setDefault("screen_w", "1024");
 	settings->setDefault("screen_h", "600");
